.TH NODEMAP.IDENTITY 4 2026-06-04 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
nodemap.identity \- human-readable identity for dynamic nodemaps
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param nodemap." NODEMAP_NAME ".identity"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 444 " | " -r--r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per nodemap (except the default nodemap).
.TP
.B Config
.br
Present for all nodemaps except the default nodemap.
.TP
.B Default
.br
Empty string.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B identity
parameter shows the human-readable identity associated with a dynamic nodemap.
Dynamic nodemaps are created automatically by certain authentication and
identity management mechanisms (such as GSS IAM) to provide fine-grained,
per-identity mapping for clients.
.PP
For static nodemaps configured via
.BR lctl-nodemap-add (8),
this parameter is always empty. For dynamic nodemaps, it contains the
string representation of the external identity (e.g., a GSS principal name)
that the nodemap was created for, up to a maximum of 1024 characters.
.PP
This parameter is read-only and is intended for debugging and administrative
monitoring to correlate dynamic nodemaps with their corresponding external
identities.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B nodemap.*.identity
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
To see the identity of a specific nodemap:
.EX
.RB "# " "lctl get_param nodemap.dynamic_123.identity"
nodemap.dynamic_123.identity=user@DOMAIN.COM
.EE
To see all nodemaps and their identities:
.EX
.RB "# " "lctl get_param nodemap.*.identity"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B nodemap.identity
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" Added in commit 2.17.5x
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lctl (8),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-nodemap-add (8)
